  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let&#39;s consider the following diagram-</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/685c633d-6f32-480f-a5d0-13db2fa8f1fa-9896603.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 225px;\" /></p><p>Let&#39;s assume that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;indicates the distances of the images of objects A and B respectively.</p><p>Thus, by mirror formula, for object A, it can be written that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnspacing=\"0px\" columnalign=\"right center left\"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>v</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>u</mi></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>f</mi></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd/><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>60</mn></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>Similarly, for object B, using mirror formula,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>20</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>25</mn></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>Hence, the distance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>d</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;between the images can be calculated as follows:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mi>d</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>160</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p>",
